### Black-box differential check

`brute_test.go` contains an independent reference that enumerates every subset (containing all responded operations) and every total order, checking real-time order and the sequential spec. `TestRandomAgainstBruteForce` runs 20 000 random multi-register histories (with pending operations and arbitrary read values) through both the reference and the optimized checker and asserts identical verdicts. All 20 000 agree, plus 17 targeted unit tests cover overlap reordering, the pivot backtracking counterexample, pending inclusion/exclusion, explicit initial values, locality and large histories.
